# Copy this file to audio-scrobbler-backup.env (same directory) and fill in
# values. It is loaded by audio-scrobbler-backup.service via EnvironmentFile
# and is NOT tracked by git (see .gitignore) since it may carry a private
# heartbeat URL.

# Where scrobbler-*.dump files are written locally before the script's own
# rclone upload runs (see GDRIVE_REMOTE_NAME in .env.production). Leave this
# unset to use the default (a `backups/` dir under the app's deploy path).
#
# Do NOT point this at another app's shared backup-sweep directory (e.g. a
# path an existing rclone/Synology cron job already pushes offsite) unless
# you've checked where that job files things upstream — on a shared host it's
# easy to end up with these dumps misfiled under a different app's remote
# folder. This app already gets its own offsite copy via the rclone block in
# backup_database.sh; there's no need to piggyback on another app's job.
#BACKUP_DIR=/srv/audio-scrobbler-app/backups

# Dead-man's-switch / heartbeat base URL (e.g. a healthchecks.io check UUID
# URL: https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>). On success the script GETs this URL as-is;
# on failure it GETs "<url>/fail". Leave unset to disable heartbeat pings.
#HEARTBEAT_URL=https://hc-ping.com/replace-with-your-check-uuid
